# The assessment of AGT-015 against this build. The requirement identifier is this
# file's stem and appears nowhere inside it, because a second place to spell the identity
# is a second place for it to be wrong -- the rule OD-SPEC-007 chose for a record
# registration, and CHK-003.assessment states for this registry.
#
# AGT-015: "Every Knowledge Integration Adapter request shall declare the subjects or task
# being contextualized, the identity and version of the consuming Nomos operation, requested
# KnowledgeSourceRole values, authority and freshness requirements, applicable repository,
# build, environment, domain, and temporal scope, contradiction handling, result and token
# budgets, permitted uses, and required provenance. Requests shall use neutral protocol
# references rather than peer-private storage identifiers."
#
# No composed "Knowledge Integration Adapter request" type exists anywhere -- confirmed by
# D-137's own text, "nothing yet produces or consumes one" -- so most of the eleven
# enumerated declaration fields have no real site to cite.
#
# The requirement's second sentence is a narrower, genuinely satisfied exception:
# `KnowledgeReferenceId` is real and tested, minted specifically so a citation to an
# external knowledge system's claim is carried as an opaque, neutral reference rather than
# reusing an existing Nomos identity or a bare peer-private string -- D-137's "Alternatives
# Considered" section explicitly rejects reusing `SchemaId` or `String` for exactly this
# reason. `OperationName` ("the only authoritative name for an operation... a CLI spelling,
# an MCP tool name... are all projections of this") is the real, tested vocabulary that
# would carry "the identity and version of the consuming Nomos operation" if a request type
# existed to hold it.
verdict: Partial
